      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It is not an inherent predisposition toward instability, but rather a difference in cultural approaches to workplace structure. In some cultures, relationships and collective harmony may take precedence over strict adherence to immediate, individual rules, which can be perceived as unpredictable from a standardized corporate viewpoint. Eastern European models often embed a stronger emphasis on formalized hierarchy and measurable process compliance from the outset. Therefore, the key difference is often in the *approach* to discipline, requiring tailored management to translate Western expectations into locally relevant operational norms.",
